Description:
	Procedure Modeling of Building, part of OpenCity project, another 3D city simulation game.

This is partial ruby implementation of "Procedural modeling of buildings" by P. Mueller.
RTFSC

Look at for withpaper:
http://www.vision.ee.ethz.ch/~pmueller/documents/mueller.procedural_modeling_of_buildings.SG2006.web-version.pdf

Some details at:
http://www.opencity.info/wiki/index.php/BuildingProceduralGenerationOverview
http://www.opencity.info/wiki/index.php/BuildingProceduralGeneration

Last modified:
	$Id$

Run
```sh
ruby rules.rb rules/canary.yml 5 3 4
ruby rules.rb rules/ttd.yml 10 30 10
ruby rules.rb rules/nyc1920.yml 20 14 8
ruby rules.rb rules/sf-central-tower.yml 10 10 10
```

Build sprite atlas from a directory of sprite images
```sh
ruby promobu/dir_sprite_pack.rb nyc1920 --out-dir . --output-base nyc1920-sprites
ruby promobu/dir_sprite_pack.rb ttd --out-dir . --output-base ttd-sprites
ruby promobu/dir_sprite_pack.rb canary --out-dir . --output-base canary-sprites
```

Build sprite atlas from SVG rect markers
```sh
ruby promobu/svg_rect_sprite.rb sf-central-tower.sprite.svg --out-dir . --output-base sf-central-tower-sprites
```
Requires ImageMagick (`magick` or `convert`) in `PATH`.

Use sprite atlas textures in rules (single image + JSON sprite frames)
```yml
textures:
	window_atlas:
		type: sprite
		file: sf-central-tower-sprites.webp
		sprites: sf-central-tower-sprites.json
		sprite: level-1-window
```

You can also keep `type: adapted` or `type: tiled` and add `sprites` + `sprite` to use atlas UVs.
Optional: set `atlas_w` and `atlas_h` to force atlas image dimensions.
